captured
Real `opencode run` against `opencode 1.18.30`, same isolation as `completed.ndjson.provenance`,
against a fake model server that accepted the connection and never answered. `SIGTERM` was sent
3 seconds in; the process exited with status 143 and produced zero bytes on stdout — not even
the `step_start` event a normal turn starts with. Empty by construction, not truncation.
